---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Cookie Policy — Unpeeragogy" description="Extended information notice on the use of cookies and similar technologies.">
  <article class="prose max-w-3xl mx-auto prose-sm">
    <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>

    <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> 28 August 2026</p>

    <p>This document describes the types of cookies and similar technologies used on this website (<code>unpeeragogy.pyragogy.org</code>).</p>

    <hr />

    <h2>1. What Are Cookies</h2>

    <p>Cookies are small text strings that websites visited by a user send to their terminal (usually the browser), where they are stored before being transmitted back to the same sites on subsequent visits.</p>

    <hr />

    <h2>2. Types of Cookies Used</h2>

    <p>This site follows a strict minimization policy and <strong>does not use profiling or advertising tracking cookies</strong>.</p>

    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Cookie Name</th>
          <th>Type</th>
          <th>Duration</th>
          <th>Purpose</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>cc_cookie</code></td>
          <td>Technical / Necessary</td>
          <td>6 months</td>
          <td>Stores the user's consent preference expressed via the cookie banner.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>theme</code></td>
          <td>Technical / Necessary</td>
          <td>Persistent (localStorage)</td>
          <td>Saves the user's visual preference (dark or light mode).</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <hr />

    <h2>3. Third-Party Services</h2>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Giscus</strong>: the comments system may set technical cookies to authenticate the user via GitHub. GitHub is an independent data controller.</li>
    </ul>

    <hr />

    <h2>4. Managing and Revoking Consent</h2>

    <p>You may at any time modify or withdraw your consent by clicking the <strong>"Manage Cookies"</strong> button in the footer of any page, or by configuring your browser settings to block or delete cookies.</p>

    <hr />

    <h2>5. Updates</h2>

    <p>This Cookie Policy may be updated periodically. The date of the latest revision is shown at the top of this document.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>